title="An Intelligent Species Level Deep Learning-Based Framework in Automatic Classification of Microscopic Bacteria Images",
booktitle="Innovations in Computational Intelligence and Computer Vision ",
year="2022",
publisher="Springer Nature Singapore",
address="Singapore",
pages="597--604",
abstract="Microorganisms play a crucial role in earth's ecosystem and contribute both positively and in negative aspect to a greater extent. Bacteria are responsible for various diseases in humans, but few bacteria species like tuberculosis, cholera, leprosy, etc. are extremely dangerous in nature. The species level classification of these microbes is very crucial in drug discovery for studying humans and plants micro biome. The manual classification of bacteria species based on phenotypic characteristics is very exhaustive and cumbersome task. The whole procedure depends on human expertise and expensive equipment. A deep learning-based bacterial image classification system can save both time and human efforts through automation of the entire process. Over the past few years, deep learning has contributed tremendously in the field of solving complex problem related to image classification. In this paper, a deep learning-based framework using convolutional neural network has been proposed to classify microscopic images of stained bacteria species. Three bacteria species: Bacillus Coagulans, Staphylococcus Aureus and Clostridium Perfringens have been undertaken for the study. The dataset consists of 900 microscopic bacterial images, which is further enhanced by applying data augmentation techniques like flipping, shearing, etc. The proposed classification model achieved training and testing accuracy of 96.75{\%} and 81.35{\%}, respectively.",
isbn="978-981-19-0475-2"
}

